2026-10-19T08:43:11.7722468Z [36;1m# --no-renames, and it is not cosmetic: a rename is reported by its[0m
2026-10-19T08:43:11.7722737Z [36;1m# DESTINATION only, so moving CLAUDE.md to RENAMED.md yields a list[0m
2026-10-19T08:43:11.7723003Z [36;1m# matching no glob and the approval gate would not fire on the change[0m
2026-10-19T08:43:11.7723267Z [36;1m# that removed a policy file. Measured both ways before wiring it.[0m
2026-10-19T08:43:11.7723554Z [36;1mgit diff --no-renames --name-only "$PR_BASE...$PR_HEAD" > /tmp/pr-files.txt[0m
2026-10-19T08:43:11.7723789Z [36;1mwc -l < /tmp/pr-files.txt[0m
2026-10-19T08:43:11.7723996Z [36;1m# The same diff less its additions: what the base already had. A[0m
2026-10-19T08:43:11.7724252Z [36;1m# reporter that grades `main` is exempt from `## Red checks` only[0m
